I'd have to disagree with that.  In typical Crack runs, over 30% of 
the passwords broken were cracked with information in the gecos field.
(name, office, phone#, etc.)  While cracking becomes far more diffi-
cult without the encrypted password, it isn't impossible to do without
it.

>Punishing a user for copying this file, which does not even contain 
>password information, is, well, extreme to the point of silliness. 

