I am a student at the University of California, San Diego.  
I am doing a research paper and need to gather data about 
persons who are participating/have participated in some form 
of environmental activism.  Some examples of environmental 
activism would be civil disobedience, participation in some 
form of educational endeavor regarding the environment, or 
just belonging to a political collective or environmental 
cause.

I am asking anyone who feels that they meet this criteria to 
respond to the following questions.  Answers can be as brief 
or as long as you would like.  Please be frank and honest.  
Do NOT respond over the net but instead E-mail with your 
responses at :

ww10bbp@issci1.ucsd.edu

Thank you for your cooperation and time.


                        Questions

1) Describe your act of "ecological activism"?  What did you 
do or what are you doing?

2) Where did you acquire your views on the environment?  For 
example, were you raised with them?  Did you learn them at 
