suspected that a copy of elm that *I* had compiled on the system was the
cause of the problem.  The sysadmin informed me that they would look at the
source code for the program, which was in my account, to try and figure out
the cause, and then decide whether I should have access to the system.

Unfortunately, this never did happen - the code was, to my best knowledge,
never looked at, and I did not get access to the system except for a short
period at the end of the semester to attempt to clear out some files.

I was unable to clear out everything, but, c'est la vie.  Maybe someday I
can get to them from somewhere else...  (With appropriate sanction..)

However, just goes to show that it does not always work out as you would
expect it to...l.

