I think that in the rush to castigate the Sysadmins at Houston we are 
forgetting the basic truth of the situation.
 
The student when he dropped the class lost permission to use THAT account.
The sysadmin gave the student an opportunity to get HIS files onto media
that he owns (which would include printouts).  
The only use the temporary account reactiviation was to be put to was to
get HIS files off that account.  He was NOT given permission to download
files that he didn't own.  Even though there are many files that can be
accessed, this student didn't OWN them.  

When a student who was only supposed to be downloading HIS files started
printing out the userlist in the form of a passwd file he was obviously
going beyond the activity he was granted in a effort to be reasonable fair
to this student.  

Now I won't argue that by continuing to state that the file might be used to
crack the system the sysadmins were trying to justify their actions.  However,
their actions were not capricious.  They were based on the fact that this
student went beyond what he agreed to do and started to obtain files that
were not his to take.  They were not owned by him, they were not within his
directory, they had no apparent use by an individual once off the system.

Plus, to this student's disadvantage, he had been involved with usage problems
in the past at this institution.  So this was the third time that his name
was brought to the attention of the sysadmins.  If he hadn't done the other
activities maybe the sysadmins wouldn't have seen him as a third time 
troublemaker.  

So to recap,  The student was given permission to download his files.  The
/etc/passwd file is not his file.  He got caught copying it to the printer
by someone who knew he shouldn't be downloading other's files.  This was
his 3rd strike.  He was out.

Marc Siskin
Senior Media Designer
Language Resource Center
University of Michigan
Msiskin@umich.edu

This post represents my personal opinion based on reading the many messages
on this subject.  I do not claim to know what was going through the minds of
any of the participants in this situation.  



