far too many grey areas where personal interpitation can have  a drastic effect 
on how the enforcment of the policy should be done. This leads to situations 
where two people will recieve different kinds of justice for performing the 
same action. That is flawed and should be corrected. In addition, the policy 
contain unmeasurable statements, or feel-goods, that base policy on the 
opinions of the policy enforcers. Any policy that allows opinion at the time to 
effect the overall policy is also flawed and should be fixed.

Finally, the students knew what they were getting when they agreed to this 
policy. There are avenues of redress that students can use to try to effect 
changes in policy. Making yourself "above" the policy you agreed to is not one 
of them.

