I don't think it's at all reasonable to ignore how he may have
acquired it.  If someone, even KC, has information, even a list of
student grades, he has the right to keep it, make copies of it, and
distribute them; that's called "freedom of the press."  It's a concept
we have here, though given your previous comments I'm not surprised
you haven't heard of it.

He could be charged with theft if such was involved in acquiring the
information, or a student whose grades were included could try to sue
for defamation or something, but that's something else.  If the
information is on a University-owned computer, they may well have the
right to delete it from his account with appropriate due process
protections (if UH has any such thing), but if he already got it off
their computer that's too bad.
